{
 "name": "Aerosoft CRJ",
 "match": [
  "CRJ",
  "ASCRJ"
 ],
 "notes": "Aerosoft CRJ 550/700/900/1000 (MSFS 2020). Its WASM owns the default sim variables (lights, trim, flaps, autopilot), so the generic switch sync for those is off: writing them on the other sim gets reverted and echoed back. Controls that fire input events (flap lever, park brake, GPWS guard, signs) sync through those; their duplicate L:vars are ignored. Classes are a best guess from the 2026-11-12 log; check them with tools/probe.py.",
 "lvars": [
  "ASCRJ_FCP_HDG_SEL",
  "ASCRJ_ELEVTRIM",
  "ASCRJ_TQ_THROTTLE_1_POS",
  "ASCRJ_TQ_THROTTLE_2_POS",
